clauses.text_en:
In this decree:
1) vapour barrier means a material layer that prevents harmful diffusion of water vapour into or within a structure;
2) air barrier means a material layer that prevents harmful airflow through a structure from one side to the other;
3) capillary flow means movement of liquid in a porous material caused by local differences in pore suction pressure;
4) moisture means water that is not chemically bound, in gaseous, liquid or solid form;
5) wet room means a room other than a habitable room whose floor is exposed to water because of its use, and whose wall surfaces may be splashed or may condense water in normal use;
6) construction moisture means moisture that entered structures or building materials during or before construction, above the building's equilibrium moisture content in use, and that must leave;
7) crawl space means an intentionally designed air space bounded by the building's floor, foundation wall and ground, ventilated to outdoor air;
8) technical service life means the time for which a structure or building part is technically able to last;
9) ventilation opening or slot means an inlet or outlet opening or slot leading from outside into the ventilation space or cavity of a structure;
10) ventilation space means a continuous air space in a structure through which the ventilation airflow passes, whose height or thickness perpendicular to the airflow direction is over 0.2 metres;
11) ventilation cavity means a continuous air gap in a structure through which the ventilation airflow passes, whose height or thickness perpendicular to the airflow direction is at most 0.2 metres;
12) waterproofing means a material layer that withstands continuous wetting and prevents harmful penetration of water into a structure;
13) water pressure insulation means a material layer that, with its seams and supporting structures, withstands the continuous water pressure requirement set for the structure and prevents harmful penetration of water under water pressure;
14) diffusion of water vapour means movement of water vapour molecules in a gas mixture at constant total pressure, tending to even out differences in vapour concentration or partial vapour pressure;
15) convection of water vapour means transfer of water vapour carried by a gas mixture as it moves under a total pressure difference;
16) water vapour resistance means, for a uniform material layer or a layered structure of such layers, the ratio of the difference in water vapour concentration or partial pressure between the two sides to the water vapour flow diffusing per unit area through the layer or structure in steady state;
17) roof covering means the structure formed by the roof cover, any underlay and the structural parts directly supporting them.
